abstract: >-
  An open, fully computational pipeline and benchmark for full-ensemble AI music
  generation. It turns free-text requests into score-like specifications (orchestration,
  dynamics, form, cultural style), compiles them into prompts or MIDI scores, and
  evaluates plain, expert and pipeline conditions with automatic metrics and an open AI
  audio judge, with SHA-256 provenance and preregistered statistics. Conducted
  independently; not an official Brunel University London project.
  AI assistance statement: This project was developed by KEYUR SHAILESHKUMAR PATEL with
  the help of an AI assistant (Claude, by Anthropic) for drafting text, writing and
  testing code, and literature search. All research decisions, the study design and the
  final content were chosen and approved by the author, who takes full responsibility
  for the work.
keywords:
  - AI music generation
  - orchestration
  - prompt engineering
  - text-to-audio
  - reproducibility
  - open science
